Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 02:16:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: flush the requests of a new output right away

createOutput() queues get_xdg_surface, get_toplevel and the initial
commit, but nothing flushed them: they went out with the next
dispatchEvents(), which only runs once the host has sent something. A host
with nothing pending (for example a headless parent without seat devices)
then never configures the toplevel, the output is never announced and the
consumer falls back to its headless output. Found by testing against a
headless sway parent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/backend/Wayland.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/backend/Wayland.cpp b/src/backend/Wayland.cpp
index b14096b..0710dba 100644
--- a/src/backend/Wayland.cpp
+++ b/src/backend/Wayland.cpp
@@ -218,6 +218,11 @@ bool Aquamarine::CWaylandBackend::createOutput(const std::string& szName) {
         backend->events.newOutput.emit(SP<IOutput>(o));
         o->announce();
     });
+
+    // Send the new toplevel's requests now. They would otherwise wait for the next dispatchEvents(),
+    // which only runs once the host has sent something: a host that says nothing until it gets them
+    // (e.g. no seat events pending) never configures the output, and it is never announced.
+    wl_display_flush(waylandState.display);
     return true;
 }
 
